      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin and 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change the limit.\n\nThe 1700 mg figure may be a typo or a total daily dose entered as a per-dose amount. Here are some options within the label:\n\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg twice or three times daily**, if you're starting or titrating.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you meant a different drug or strength, tell me that instead."
      }
